  ------------------------------------------------------------
    what you see
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      dusk. a flooded marsh. small parties arrive,

      0:24   the pour: thousands rain out of the high sky
      0:38   a funnel dips to the water
      0:48   the falcon: a dart tears the crowd in two
      1:04   the spectacle: the panic wave, braided strands
      1:52   night. the whole sky comes down to roost
      2:08   end

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome, wait for the
      title screen to finish loading, then click.
      No server, no flags. ESC leaves fullscreen.
      A discrete GPU is recommended. Tested on an RTX 5090.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how it is made
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      - the flock is a metaball field shredded by noise; birds
        live one per hash cell, so the march costs a few hash
        lookups per step, never per bird
      - dense regions saturate into a silhouette, sparse fringes
        stay granular; the falcon subtracts a moving wake, and
        the panic wave is a ring of density rolling out of it
      - dusk sky, sun, cirrus and stars are analytic; the water
        reflects by a plane bounce that re-marches the flock
      - the soundtrack is a fragment shader: one pixel per
        sample at 48 kHz, 120 BPM, felt piano and pad, a kick
        and kit for the spectacle, and a synthesised starling
        chorus whose loudness follows the size of the flock
      - packed with zopfli into an HTML comment and unpacked by
        DecompressionStream, so it runs from file://

      Source, build tools and notes are in this folder; see
      readme.md.

